@title Walk-in refrigerator alarm
@subtitle Runbook for volunteers, Sunset Valley Food Share
@author Operations Manager
@date 2026-11-01

kpi Alarm limit | above 41 °F | display reading | bad
kpi Hard stop | above 45 °F | discard
kpi Ops Manager | Delphine Okonkwo

!!! Never taste or sniff food to decide whether it is safe.

Use this when the alarm sounds or the display reads above 41 °F.

## First two minutes

1. Silence the alarm.
2. Check the door is fully closed.
3. Read the display and the backup thermometer inside.
4. Write the time on the log sheet.

## Decide what to do

table = situation,what to do; "41 to 45 °F, above 41 for less than 2 hours","Move dairy, eggs, meat and prepared meals into the backup chest freezers right away. Keep produce in place. Call the refrigeration technician."; "Above 45 °F, or above 41 for 2 hours or more, or nobody knows how long","**Throw away** dairy, eggs, meat and prepared meals, with a second volunteer present to confirm. Produce, canned and packaged goods can stay."

## Steps in order

1. Call ChillRight, the refrigeration vendor, on 555-0134 (open 24 hours) and ask for a 4-hour response.
2. Message the Operations Manager.
3. Move or discard items as above.
4. Record each item thrown away on the waste log with its weight in pounds.
5. After the repair, run the refrigerator for 4 hours below 38 °F before restocking.

## Contacts

table = role,name; Operations Manager,Delphine Okonkwo; ChillRight on-call line,555-0134; Food safety lead,Bram Verhoeven
